.Dd August 28, 2026
.Dt SIMSALABIM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm simsalabim
.Nd headless control for the Simsalabim suite
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm status
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm mode
.Ar module
.Ar mode
.Op Fl -launch
.Nm
.Cm seed
.Op Fl -contacts
.Op Fl -calendar
.Op Fl -reminders
.Op Fl -photos
.Op Fl -device Ar udid
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility drives a running
.Pa Simsalabim.app
instance — the macOS menu bar suite that retrofits the iOS Simulator with
real Bluetooth, camera, and NFC hardware, plus seeded Contacts, Calendar,
Reminders, and Photos data — from the command line, for scripting and CI.
.Pp
.Ic status
and
.Ic mode
talk to Simsalabim.app over a local control socket at
.Pa /tmp/simsalabim.sock ,
so the app must already be running, or be started with
.Fl -launch .
.Ic seed
drives the simulator directly and does
.Em not
require Simsalabim.app to be running — in fact it must not be, since both
bind the same
.Pa /tmp/simulacrum.sock .
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic status Op Fl -json
Prints each hardware module's current mode
.Pq Sy impossible , Sy camouflage , Sy nfcromancer
and whether it is mid-transition.
With
.Fl -json ,
prints the raw response object instead of a table.
.It Ic mode Ar module Ar mode Op Fl -launch
Switches one module to
.Ar mode
on the running Simsalabim.app.
.Ar module
is one of
.Sy impossible , Sy camouflage , Sy nfcromancer ;
.Ar mode
is one of
.Sy off , Sy mock , Sy passthrough .
The call blocks until the transition settles, or the request fails after a
10-second timeout.
With
.Fl -launch ,
starts Simsalabim.app first if it is not already running, and waits up to
15 seconds for it to become reachable.
.It Ic seed
Seeds a booted simulator with the fixture Simulacrum's own UI stores at
.Pa ~/Library/Application\~Support/Simulacrum/fixture.json .
With no category flag
.Po
.Fl -contacts , Fl -calendar , Fl -reminders , Fl -photos
.Pc
given, seeds every category.
Without
.Fl -device Ar udid ,
targets the single booted simulator — an error if there are zero or more
than one.
With
.Fl -json ,
prints the finished summary as JSON instead of plain text.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/tmp/simulacrum.sock"
.It Pa /tmp/simsalabim.sock
Control socket for
.Ic status
and
.Ic mode .
Owned by Simsalabim.app while it runs; one connection per request.
.It Pa /tmp/simulacrum.sock
Seed-agent socket used by
.Ic seed
and by Simsalabim.app's own Simulacrum module — only one owner at a time.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 64
Invalid
.Ar module No / Ar mode
argument, or an ambiguous
.Ic seed
device selection (multiple booted simulators and no
.Fl -device ) .
.It 69
Simsalabim.app is not reachable and
.Fl -launch
was not passed, or
.Fl -launch
timed out.
.It 70
The control socket reported failure, a mode transition timed out, or
.Ic seed
failed — including being blocked by a Simsalabim.app that is already
running.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Show current modes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ simsalabim status
impossible: off
camouflage: mock
nfcromancer: off
.Ed
.Pp
Switch ImpossiBLE to passthrough, starting the app first if needed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ simsalabim mode impossible passthrough --launch
.Ed
.Pp
Seed contacts and calendar events into a specific simulator:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ simsalabim seed --contacts --calendar \e
    --device 1E2C3B4A-5678-90AB-CDEF-1234567890AB
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr defaults 1 ,
.Xr xcrun 1
.Sh CAVEATS
.Ic mode
and
.Ic status
only see a running Simsalabim.app; they do not read or write
.Xr defaults 1
directly, since the app itself reads its defaults domain exactly once, at
launch.
.Pp
.Ic seed
and a running Simsalabim.app cannot seed at the same time — both bind
.Pa /tmp/simulacrum.sock ,
and the second one to start loses.
